From c7f280893b5ddedf5f433b0997358648d778b286 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Zenolith\\zen" <johnnyzen@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 12:25:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Wine: skip IsValidLocale check on Android in Global_SetLocale

Regression introduced when adopting upstream's full Global_SetLocale
implementation in commit 83bfd53 (Wine 10.19 -> 11.8 upgrade). Upstream
now validates the LCID via IsValidLocale(LCID_INSTALLED), which on
Android always returns FALSE because our NLS-data shims (locale.c) make
find_lcid_entry return NULL.

Result: every table that calls SetLocale 1033 (the standard line in
every VPW init) failed with VBSE_LOCALE_SETTING_NOT_SUPPORTED, which
cascaded through vpmInit and surfaced as TYPE_MISMATCH on gBOT(s).Z
later in the script. Affected: PinBot, Lord of the Rings VPW 1.6,
Lethal Weapon 3 VPW 2.0, World Cup Soccer VPW v1.2, Harlem Globetrotters
VPW 1.0 (5 of 14 tables in the 2026-05-07 crash batch).

Wrap the IsValidLocale check in #ifndef __STANDALONE__ so the standalone
build skips validation and accepts whatever LCID the script asks for.
The lcid is still written to the script context below the check, so the
script-visible behaviour matches the pre-upgrade B-26 shim that
unconditionally returned S_OK.

All 5 affected tables verified playable after this fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 standalone/inc/wine/dlls/vbscript/global.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/standalone/inc/wine/dlls/vbscript/global.c b/standalone/inc/wine/dlls/vbscript/global.c
index efd316881..63a178ad2 100644
--- a/standalone/inc/wine/dlls/vbscript/global.c
+++ b/standalone/inc/wine/dlls/vbscript/global.c
@@ -2714,8 +2714,15 @@ static HRESULT Global_SetLocale(BuiltinDisp *This, VARIANT *args, unsigned args_
         }
         }
 
+#ifndef __STANDALONE__
         if(!IsValidLocale(new_lcid, LCID_INSTALLED))
             return MAKE_VBSERROR(VBSE_LOCALE_SETTING_NOT_SUPPORTED);
+#endif
+        /* On Android our NLS-data shims make IsValidLocale always return
+         * FALSE, which would reject every SetLocale 1033 call (the standard
+         * VPW init line). Skip the validation and accept whatever LCID the
+         * script asks for; the lcid is recorded into the script context
+         * below either way. */
     }
 
     This->ctx->lcid = new_lcid;
-- 
