From 7080fb926d2d59944a1a033ba2ad043355607b81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Zenolith\\zen" <johnnyzen@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 22:43:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] EM tables: fix Controller binding + B2SSetData overload +
 FormatNumber
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Standalone build was crashing on EM tables (WoZ, FORGE, etc.) at the
first Controller method call. Five layered issues; all fixed:

DynamicScript: type-aware overload resolution
  Was matching by arg count only ("FIXME match overload on type and
  arguments"). Two B2SSetData overloads — (int,int) and (string,int) —
  always picked the first registered. Script call with a string arg
  hit DISP_E_TYPEMISMATCH. Now scores each candidate by category match
  (string→string +10, numeric→numeric +10, mismatched 0) and picks the
  best, falling back to first-registered on ties. Affects every plugin
  with overloaded same-arity methods, not just B2S.

Wine vbscript: graceful NLS fallback in format_number_lcid /
format_currency_lcid
  Android's NLS shim returns 0 from GetNumberFormatW for many inputs
  (NlsValidateLocale incomplete). Was returning DISP_E_TYPEMISMATCH;
  now falls back to the raw to_string() result. Matches the pattern
  already in oleaut32/vartype.c:6529.

Wine vbscript: to_int leniency for whitespace/empty BSTRs
  MS VBScript silently coerces "        " → 0; Wine errored. Buggy
  community scripts (WoZ ExpandLine: Left(s, Space(n))) hit this.
  Whitespace-only strings now return 0; non-whitespace garbage still
  propagates the error so real bugs aren't masked.

ScriptArrayList shim
  System.Collections.ArrayList isn't shipped with Wine on Android.
  Many tables CreateObject("System.Collections.ArrayList") for dynamic
  ID lists. Implements the methods scripts actually use (Add/Item/
  Count/Clear/Contains/IndexOf/Remove/RemoveAt/Insert/Sort/Reverse/
  ToArray/Clone) plus IEnumVARIANT for `For Each`. Wired through
  external_create_object in def.cpp.

def.cpp::external_create_object IUnknown** fix
  Caller passes the address of a pointer typed as `IUnknown*`. Casting
  `&obj` only wrote to a local stack copy — the caller never saw the
  real object on success. Cast the parameter itself back to IUnknown**.
  Was harmless on failure paths but silently broken for ArrayList.

Diagnostic gating
  Adds external_diag_enabled() (env VPX_SCRIPT_DIAG=1) and the macros
  EXTERNAL_LOG_DIAG / PLOGI_DIAG / PLOGE_DIAG / PLOGW_DIAG. ~20
  [CTRL-DIAG] log sites covering Wine dispatch, plugin object creation,
  controller.vbs flow, FormatNumber, GetTextFile resolution, and
  B2SLegacy factory invocation are now off by default. See
  reference_vpx_script_diag.md for usage.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
