From 10d4e146751191bd1a92ecbeb8cc43addd38a9c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Zenolith\\zen" <johnnyzen@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 20:37:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Misc Android fixes: web server reconnect, BGFX shutdown
 safety, ResURIResolver stale-this guard, log noise

Web server: skip down / link-local interfaces in GetIPAddress (IFF_RUNNING +
IFF_UP + 169.254/16 filter so airplane-mode cached wlan0 IPs and unrouteable
addresses no longer surface as the server URL). Adds WebServer::RefreshUrl
and the VPinballRefreshWebServer host API (C + JNI) so the host can re-emit
VPINBALL_EVENT_WEB_SERVER after a Wi-Fi reconnect without restarting the
server. The listening socket is bound to 0.0.0.0 so it survives DHCP renewal;
only m_url goes stale.

Plugin ResURIResolver: track live instances in a static s_liveResolvers set;
each callback (OnDisplaySrcChanged et al.) checks it before dereferencing
userData. Works around MsgPluginManager::UnsubscribeMsg matching by callback
function pointer only - with multiple resolvers (Player, B2SRenderer,
ScoreView, B2SLegacy::Form) sharing the same static callbacks, an unsubscribe
can erase the wrong subscription, leaving a freed `this` in the subscriber
list. Observed crash: FlexDMD dtor broadcasts OnDmdSrcChanged at table-exit,
fans out to a Player-owned resolver that has already been freed.

Renderer: introduce std::atomic<bool> g_bgfxIsAlive in RenderDevice.cpp, false
before bgfx::init / after bgfx::shutdown. Sampler::~Sampler returns early
when clear so the BGFX-handle destroy is skipped on samplers whose owners
outlived the context (m_pendingTextureUploads, RenderTarget samplers,
Shader::m_samplers cache, plugin caches). Eliminates the
pthread_mutex_lock @ NULL+0x1c0 SIGSEGV on app exit. bgfx::isValid does not
catch this because it only compares the handle to kInvalidHandle.

Crash handler (vpinball_sigsegv_handler): walk the stack via _Unwind_Backtrace
after recording the ucontext PC, so the watchdog gets the caller chain
instead of just pthread_mutex_lock / memcpy / similar terminal frames.

Logger: drop the vpinball.log RollingFileAppender on Android. The host
crash reporter pulls from logcat (VPinballCrashReportCapture.kt) and no
in-app code reads the file, so the per-call disk flush was pure overhead.

Input: register staged-flipper touch regions alongside the primary flippers
(left + right zones now fire both Left/Right + StagedLeft/StagedRight, so
tables that read staged inputs work in touch mode). Collapse the
per-touch-device PLOGI into one summary line at startup. Demote
PushTouchEvent and SDL_FINGER per-event logs to PLOGD.

Audio: demote AudioDiag PLOGI lines to PLOGD across SDL + AAudio backends
(only useful with diag enabled). Demote the AudioStreamPlayer "stream sync
lost and reseted" line. Demote startup "Audio device initialized" boilerplate.

Misc log noise: MsgPluginManager plugin-loaded success boilerplate, ScoreView
per-layout parse line, simplescriptpatcher banner separators - all PLOGI to
PLOGD. Cuts Android startup log volume noticeably.

